    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div class=\"gmail_quote\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div><div>My issue is how best to include these interactions so that I can interpret the results correctly. As it stands, I have included <span>included only ONE dummy picking up each 2x2 interaction</span></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>If you already calculated your product terms as new variables in the <font face=\"courier new, monospace\">data.frame</font>, that is correct.  </div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/cat.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/cat.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792420756701000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0tjjWrauLQgQ0hbd2XGKA4\">https://lavaan.ugent.be/tutorial/cat.html</a><br></div><div><br></div><div>But you could also use the colon operator as a shortcut:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Latent1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> U1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> C1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> F1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">SESHigh</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">SHigh</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> U1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">C1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> U1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">F1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">SESHigh</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">F1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> C1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">F1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">SHigh</span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">F1</span></div></code></div><br></div><div>FYI, you have an extra tilde after Latent1 and Learner.</div><div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0px 0px 0px 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\"><div><div><span>then I&#39;m not sure how to interpret the results when that product term is significant. </span></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div><div>Probe the interaction.  </div><div><br></div><div><a href=\"http://quantpsy.org/interact/interactions.htm\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://quantpsy.org/interact/interactions.htm&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792420756701000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0N1COHEitomf25aAONn7V-\">http://quantpsy.org/interact/interactions.htm</a></div><div><br></div><div>You can <span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,0)\">label</span> the paths and calculate user-defined parameters that represent the conditional effects you want to test.  For example, if <span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\">U1</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:</span><span style=\"font-family:monospace;background-color:rgb(250,250,250);color:rgb(0,0,0)\">C1</span> is significant, and you want to probe the effect of U1 for each level of C1:</div><div><br></div><div style=\"border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">Latent1</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">~</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,0)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">b_u1</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">*</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">U1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,0)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">b_c1</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">*</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">C1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> F1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">SESHigh</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,0,102)\">SHigh</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,0)\"><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">b_int</span></span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">*</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\">U1xC1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">...</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br><br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0)\">## user-defined parameters to probe interaction</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br></span><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0)\"># </span><b><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0)\">b_u1 is already the effect of U1 when C1 == 0 (and F1 == 0)</span></b><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"><br>b_u1_c1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">:=</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> b_u1 </span><span style=\"color:rgb(102,102,0)\">+</span><span style=\"color:rgb(0,0,0)\"> b_int </span><b><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0)\"># effect of U1 when C1 == 1</span></b><b><span style=\"color:rgb(136,0,0)\"> (and F1 == 0)</span></b></div></code></div><div><br></div><div><br></div><div><div><div>Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div>Assistant Professor, Methods and Statistics</div><div>Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792420756701000&amp;usg=AOvVaw2rl0uK1KZyzu6joN-2ceYf\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div></div><div><br></div></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p></blockquote></div>"
